001100 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
001200 PROGRAM-ID.          TCUMRCV.
001300 AUTHOR.              LYNN M BUNN.
001400 DATE-WRITTEN.        NOVEMBER 1982.
001500 DATE-COMPILED.
001600*INSTALLATION.        GOODYEAR TIRE AND RUBBER - AKRON.
001700*SECURITY.
001800*REMARKS.
001900*
002000*         C U M B E R L A N D ' S    R E C E I V I N G   P G M
002100*
002200*        PROCESSING OUTLINE:
002300*        1.  THE INPUT FROM CUMBERLAND IS READ.
002400*        2.  IF THE RECEIVING RECORD IS AN ORIGINAL:
002500*            A)  MPORCV     PUT      NEW RS ENTRY (' ' IN STATUS)
002600*            IF CODED ITEM:
002700*            B)  DPOITEM    UPDATE   QTY DLVR, DATE DLVR
002800*                           PUT      NEW RS PER ITEM
002900*            C)  DVENDITM   PUT      IF NO SEGMENT EXISTS
003000*                           UPDATE   LEAD TIME.
003100*            D)  MSTORERM   UPDATE   ONORDER, LAST DLVRTIME
003200*                                    UNPAID QTY, ACTIVITY DATE
003300*            IF NON-CODED ITEM:
003400*            B)  DPONSITM   UPDATE   QTY DLVR, DATE DLVR
003500*                           PUT      NEW RS PER ITEM.
003600*
003700*        3.  IF THE RECEIVING RECORD IS A CORRECTION:
003800*            IF CODED ITEM:
003900*            A)  DPOITEM    UPDATE   QTY DLVR, DATE DLVR
004000*            B)  MSTORERM   UPDATE   ONORDER, UNPAID QUANTITY
004100*            IF NON-CODED ITEM:
004200*            A)  DPONSITM   UPDATE   QTY DLVR, DATE DLVR
004300*
004400*        4.  A RECEIVING ERROR REPORT IS PRINTED.
004500*
004600*    NOTE1:  BCUMRCV:  COBOL STREAM.
004700*            BXCUMRCV: JOB   STREAM.
004800*
004900*    NOTE2:  RECEIVING SLIP CORRECTION RECORDS LOOK EXACTLY
005000*            LIKE THE ORIGINAL RECEIVING SLIP RECORD.  IF
005100*            THE QUANTITIES ARE THE SAME, NO PROCESSING WILL
005200*            BE DONE; OTHERWISE THE NEW QUANTITY WILL REPLACE
005300*            THE OLD QUANTITY.
005400*
005500*    NOTE3:  THE CODED RECORDS WILL ALWAYS BE RECEIVED IN THE
005600*            STOREROOM UM.  (THEREFORE NO CONVERSIONS NEED TO
005700*            BE DONE).
005800*
005900*            ABOVE NOTE IS NOT ENTIRELY CORRECT.  IF PO UM IS
006000*            DIFFERENT FROM STOREROOM UM, A CONVERSION WILL
006100*            NEED TO BE DONE|  -B.WINTER (JULY 1984)
006200*
006300*    ON APRIL 22, 1983, THE ERROR CHECK FOR CODE FROZEN FOR
006400*            INVENTORY WAS TAKEN OUT; THE DATE AND TIME WAS
006500*            ADDED TO THE ERROR REPORT, AS WELL AS NEW HEAD-
006600*            INGS.  LMB.
006700*
006800*    ON OCTOBER 17, 1983, THE BLOW-UP DISPLAY MESSAGES WERE
006900*            ADDED.  LMB.
007000*
007100*    ON APRIL 2, 1984, ADDED ANOTHER EDIT CHECK.  IF THE MPORCV
007200*            STATUS FOR A CODED RECEIVER IS "XX" (MEANING THE
007300*            RECEIVER HAS BEEN COMPLETELY RECEIVED AND STORED),
007400*            THEN NO PROCESSING WILL BE DONE WITH THE RECORD.
007500*            THE RECORD AND AN ERROR MESSAGE WILL PRINT OUT.
007600*            LMB.
007700*
007800*    ON JUNE 6, 1984, FIXED UM EDIT CHECK FOR RECEIVING RECORD.
007900*            PREVIOUSLY WAS ALLOWING ANY UM, NOW ONLY ALLOWS
008000*            STOREROOM UM.   CAK.
008100*
008200*
008300*    ON APRIL 10, 1985; ADDED SEQUENCE CHECK FOR SENDING RECORDS.
008400*             B. WINTER.
008500*
008600*    ON APRIL 9, 1986; ALLOWED RECEIVING UM TO BE STOREROOM UM OR
008700*            ALTERNATE UMS. (AGAIN|)  B. WINTER.
008800*
008900*    ON JUNE 4, 1986; ADDED SEQUENCE NUMBER TO MPORCV.  ZEROED IT
009000*                     OUT FOR EVERYTHING. NOT USED.  B. WINTER.
009100
009200 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
